{"seq":17,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/claude-code-opus-minimal-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T06:29:11.313Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"0b03c6a51021ecb0b58e327bb45ef65cc08164f4744cd74d32d9ba334e36c17b","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through Moss's notes that are shared in the North and Central team digest folders. Two ticket numbers on Quarrendon Freight Lines turned up:\n\n• *#PD-4492*, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because the gatehouse kiosk at the Eau Claire yard wasn't sending SMS bay assignments to drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 on the 04:00 shift. Support patched the SMS gateway routing at 19:30 that day, and Thea confirmed the 5 Oct shift got through without manual help. The note also has an action item to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea filed this one because the gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on third shift. The cheat sheet says it went to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing. The note has no date, so I can't tell you when that happened.\n\nThings to watch for:\n• Neither QFL ticket appears in Moss's other two North digests (14 Sep 2025 pipeline and 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in).\n• Tickets #4409 and #4412 and request FR-882 in Moss's Central handoff digest belong to Marrow, not QFL.\n• Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company that isn't our customer, and Moss didn't write it.\n\nI can only see the Moss notes that are public files. If Moss keeps private notes, I can't see them, so I can't promise this is the full list."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":18,"trial_id":"prompt-archaeology-2026-11/claude-code-opus-minimal-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r2","wall_ts":"2026-11-04T06:29:16.923Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"ad2218115e1bd872851b15d99accb821e7dfec78b9befdb4a7b55fa278d7f7c4","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","text":"I sent you the list in this DM. Moss's notes have two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n- **#PD-4492** is in Moss's \"Sunday prep for Ruth\" digest, dated 5 Oct 2025. Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because the gatehouse kiosk at the Eau Claire yard wasn't texting bay assignments to drivers at Dock Doors 14–18 on the 04:00 shift. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the next morning's shift got through without manual help.\n- **#4419** is in Moss's \"North cheat sheet\", which has no date. Thea filed it because the gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on third shift. The cheat sheet says it went to tier-2 support for firmware testing, but I can't tell when.\n\nThings to watch for:\n- Tickets #4409 and #4412 and request FR-882 are in Moss's Central handoff digest, but they belong to Marrow, not Quarrendon.\n- Marcus has a note on \"Quarendon Freightways\", which is a different company and not our customer. Moss didn't write it.\n- Moss's other two North digests (14 Sep 2025 and 23 Mar 2026) mention Quarrendon but have no ticket numbers.\n\nI could only search Moss's notes that everyone can see in the shared files. If Moss keeps private notes, I couldn't check them, so this may not be the full list."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DPROMPT0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
